{"status":"completed","summary":"Published node1’s approved release tree as the read-only rsync module `releases`. Node2 retrieved the complete tree with modes and symlinks intact. Uploads, traversal, and non-exported private-tree access are denied. Both nodes retained CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 and recovered successfully after individual restarts.","actions_performed":["Configured a chrooted, read-only rsync daemon module on node1.","Restricted TCP/873 to node2 and enabled the daemon through native SysV startup.","Retrieved and verified the release tree on node2 using archive and whole-file transfer.","Verified write denial, path confinement, and private-module denial.","Restarted node1 and node2 sequentially and verified changed boot identities and full recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Read-only `releases` module published and persistent on node1","command_ids":["cmd-d918e7ac9ded4082","cmd-f051fca5fc4848f6","cmd-6b13c05b005e4ead","cmd-af4e7710c0a44e91"],"summary":"Configuration maps only the releases tree, enables chroot/read-only controls, restricts the firewall to node2, and shows the daemon running after restart."},{"requirement":"Node2 retrieved the full tree with modes and symlinks intact","command_ids":["cmd-09889a9c73584b03","cmd-3db7b868a81942f7"],"summary":"All six entries were retrieved; both files transferred in full, hashes match, executable mode is 0755, and `current` remains a symlink to `v1`."},{"requirement":"Writes and access outside the module tree are denied","command_ids":["cmd-36302a9aaf174124","cmd-3db7b868a81942f7"],"summary":"Uploads fail with `module is read only`; traversal remains confined and fails; the private sibling is not exported."},{"requirement":"Approved release, installed OS release, and kernel preserved","command_ids":["cmd-af4e7710c0a44e91","cmd-9bb23b45cb364708"],"summary":"Final hashes match on both nodes; CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 remain installed."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-d918e7ac9ded4082","cmd-b668451747f543c8","cmd-afe8dd24aa294a8a","cmd-4bffd5aaf65c4626","cmd-753ac4f5ee4743cf","cmd-9cc00d2804594938"],"summary":"Healthy baseline and old boot ID, reboot acknowledgement and observed outage, changed boot ID, restored daemon/firewall/data, and successful post-restart transfer are captured."},{"requirement":"Node2 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-aca677581ea94678","cmd-2af5bd4101cd4e2f","cmd-65c48367dd434aec","cmd-06c37478e757475c","cmd-3db7b868a81942f7"],"summary":"Healthy baseline and old boot ID, reboot acknowledgement and disconnect, changed boot ID, intact local data, successful fresh retrieval, and repeated access-control tests are captured."}]}
